      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A comparison was made between the analgesic, antispastic and sedative action of two associations whose only difference lay in the fact that in the second amobarbital had been replaced by diphenhydramine to withdraw possible side-effects of the barbiturate. The results obtained in patients with various diseases and a constant picture of pain and/or spasm and signs of unsettledness made it clear that both associations have much the same therapeutic action."},
